{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAHC327w5sci2GHryuMh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 2 (Sb fraction 0.225). It gave the highest EQE I measured, but it's probably not the best composition on the line. It was also the only measurement that stood out from noise.\n\nI used all 5 EQE measurements:\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0.225 | **0.0186** |\n| 8 | 0.365 | 0.0010 |\n| 13 | 0.519 | −0.0020 |\n| 17 | 0.641 | 0.0022 |\n| 23 | 0.781 | −0.0050 |\n\n**What went wrong:** I started at the middle of the line, around Sb 0.5, where the FeSbO₄ phase should sit. Three of my five measurements went there, and all read as noise. That left only two measurements for the ends. The Fe-rich sample was the one that responded, but by then I had one measurement left and spent it on the Sb-rich end, which also read as noise.\n\n**What this means:** The signal points to the Fe-rich end. My guess is that it comes from an iron-oxide-rich phase mixture, but I didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements, so the phases are unconfirmed. Indices 0 and 1 (Sb 0.189 and 0.207) are richer in Fe than index 2 and were never measured. The true best composition could well be there, or near index 2."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":414,"cache_read_input_tokens":6515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":414},"output_tokens":458,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2151889-ffce-4d89-a5f3-0ecb5125c078","uuid":"a3218bc3-2959-47ac-b06e-0b8fa81d0b52","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:33:10.036Z","request_id":"req_011CfAHC2X6qX7AySX7MPLz8"}
